body:
RESTART NOTICE RULE for the remote pilot (Greg via Engram::Advisor b9d13887 #1085, 2026-10-17 21:25:35Z), verbatim: "Oczywiście. Jak będzie nowy build, zrestartuje na Windows i Mac." When a new TermAl build needs to go live, the TermAl coordinator sends Greg (through Engram::Advisor) a concise RESTART-NOW notice containing:
- the build hash;
- the affected host(s): Windows A and/or MacBookPro B;
- the reason;
- the safe timing (no host-tracked gate of either project running).
Greg performs the Windows and MacBookPro restarts. Agents never restart, stop or start either host. This extends CLAUDE.md's existing restart rule (coordinators choose the moment; Greg performs it) to the Mac satellite.

Two-project restart notice detail preserved from full-read greg-urgent-test-runners-2026-11-03 r9 (Fable2's Nov3 19:42Z operational direction; Engram::Fable own-full second reading b229b85a-eaba-44f1-a59c-762f0bdf9233 requested preservation): when a joint restart brings both projects' prepared builds live, the notice includes BOTH TermAl's and Engram's build identities/hashes, naming affected hosts and reason; do not substitute the installed file for evidence of the image actually running after restart. This is notice/evidence content, not authority to install or restart; AGENTS and the current agreed moment still govern.
